@startuml
title Bridge / (Handle/Body)

skinparam legendBackgroundColor #f9f9f9
skinparam legendBorderColor #999999

legend right

**Intent**:
Decouple abstraction from implementation so both vary independently.

**Motivation**:
Need to avoid a combinatorial explosion of subclasses
(e.g., shapes vs. rendering APIs).

**Applicability**:
Multiply-dimension variability (e.g., device type × protocol).
Stable abstraction with changing implementations.

**Participants**:
Abstraction maintains Implementor reference; delegates work.

**Consequences**:
Pros: Independently extensible hierarchies; reduces subclass explosion.
Cons: Slight complexity; careful lifecycle coordination.

**Implementation Notes**:
Inject implementor; support switching at runtime if needed.
Different from Adapter: planning variability upfront.

**Known Uses**:
GUI toolkit look-and-feel separation; JDBC Driver vs higher-level abstractions.

**Related Patterns**:
Adapter, Strategy (algorithm selection), Abstract Factory (create implementors).

endlegend

interface Implementor {
  +operationImpl()
}

class ConcreteImplementorA
class ConcreteImplementorB
Implementor <|.. ConcreteImplementorA
Implementor <|.. ConcreteImplementorB

abstract class Abstraction {
  -impl : Implementor
  +operation()
}
class RefinedAbstraction

Abstraction <|-- RefinedAbstraction
Abstraction o-- Implementor
@enduml